{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VjCnjLWhBdos757aGyWaPA","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-52e0_8od\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 18:09 .\ndrwx------@ 13695 brenn  staff  438240 Oct  2 18:09 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    13 brenn  staff     416 Oct  2 12:20 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    6124 Oct  2 18:09 sheet.md\n# Gap hunt: B02 — Least-privilege access\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for B02:** Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Test that an allowed read works. Test that an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and a request for another tenant's data all fail. Limit each token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard permissions and permissions inherited from people.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## B02.1\n\n**Check:** The agent's IAM policy or role names specific actions and resources, with no `*` action or resource and no owner, editor, or cluster-admin role.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find IAM and RBAC files (`*.tf`, `iam*.json`, `Role`, `ClusterRoleBinding`, `RoleBinding`, CloudFormation). 2) Find the policy attached to the agent's identity. 3) Answer no if any `Action` or `Resource` is `*` or a service wildcard (`s3:*`), or it binds `roles/owner`, `roles/editor`, `cluster-admin`, or AdministratorAccess. Answer unknown if the agent's IAM is not in this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No IAM, Role or RoleBinding for the agent is in this repo (serviceaccount.yaml defines only the account); grants live in the platform or STS.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## B02.2\n\n**Check:** Tenant scope is enforced in the credential or the data layer (token claim, row-level security, or per-tenant account), not by the prompt or by code the model's output controls.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find how queries and API calls pick a tenant (search `tenant`, `org_id`, row-level security, `CREATE POLICY`, per-tenant credentials). 2) Trace where the tenant value comes from. 3) Answer no if one shared login or key reaches all tenants and the tenant ID comes from the prompt, a tool argument the model fills, or app code filtering after the query.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Tenant comes from the verified token claim (main.py:150) and no row-level security exists in migrations; memory_read takes a model-supplied business_unit, filed under R05.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## B02.3\n\n**Check:** Tokens are issued with a set audience, and receiving services reject tokens whose audience does not match.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find token requests (`audience`, `aud`, `resource`, `scope`, token client setup). 2) Find token validation in receiving services (`verify`, `jwt.decode`, middleware). 3) Answer no if tokens are requested without an audience, validation skips `aud` (`verify_aud=False`, no audience option), or accepts a list or wildcard. Answer unknown if receiving services are outside this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Tokens request an audience (identity.py:106) but the receiving gateway, payments API and Slack proxy validation is outside this repo.\n\n(no evidence cited)\n\n## B02.4\n\n**Check:** The agent uses its own service identity, not a human user's token, a copied session, or an admin key.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find where the agent loads credentials (env vars, `credentials`, `token`, `Authorization`, service account settings). 2) Check they belong to a service or workload identity for the agent. 3) Answer no if it uses a user's OAuth or session token, a personal access token, an admin or root key, or forwards the calling user's token to tools.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/identity.py:92 — \"return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Agent uses its projected service account token, not a user token\n\n`app/identity.py` lines 80–104 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  80      value: str\n  81      expires_at: float\n  82  \n  83  \n  84  @dataclass\n  85  class TokenBroker:\n  86      \"\"\"Exchanges the workload token for audience-bound access tokens.\"\"\"\n  87  \n  88      settings: Settings\n  89      _cache: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _CachedToken] = field(default_factory=dict)\n  90  \n  91      def _workload_token(self) -> str:\n  92>         return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n  93  \n  94      async def token_for(self, audience: str, scope: str, ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n  95          key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n  96          cached = self._cache.get(key)\n  97          if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n  98              return cached.value\n  99          async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client:\n 100              resp = await client.post(\n 101                  self.settings.sts_url,\n 102                  data={\n 103                      \"grant_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n 104                      \"subject_token\": self._workload_token(),\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B02.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B02\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B02.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/app\nagent/app/killswitch.py\nagent/app/ingest.py\nagent/app/startup.py\nagent/app/tools\nagent/app/tools/payments.py\nagent/app/tools/erp.py\nagent/app/tools/memory.py\nagent/app/tools/documents.py\nagent/app/tools/__init__.py\nagent/app/tools/slack.py\nagent/app/audit.py\nagent/app/approvals.py\nagent/app/budget.py\nagent/app/__init__.py\nagent/app/extractor.py\nagent/app/redact.py\nagent/app/gate.py\nagent/app/loop.py\nagent/app/settings.py\nagent/app/context_size.py\nagent/app/mcp_client.py\nagent/app/main.py\nagent/app/identity.py\nagent/config\nagent/config/policy.yaml\nagent/config/tools.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/deploy\nagent/deploy/k8s\nagent/deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/kyverno-verify-images.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/serviceaccount.yaml\nagent/deploy/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\nagent/pyproject.toml\nagent/tests\nagent/tests/test_redact.py\nagent/tests/test_gate.py\nagent/tests/fixtures\nagent/tests/fixtures/vendor_docs\nagent/tests/fixtures/vendor_docs/northwind_quote_Q4-2026.txt\nagent/tests/test_budget.py\nagent/release\nagent/release/manifest.yaml\nagent/README.md\nagent/.github\nagent/.github/workflows\nagent/.github/workflows/ci.yaml\nagent/prompts\nagent/prompts/